{
  "name": "lean-pooled-h10-fill-label",
  "notes": "Fill-window relabel of the lean pooled LightGBM lattice walk (the P16 winner, run hash 0f483677, fold docs lean-pooled-h10-wf-*). Identical pipeline, cohort, inner HPO and schedule; the ONE change is label_entry_offset_bars=1 on every scan node, so the label is close[t+1] -> close[t+1+h] (SPY-residual, vol-scaled at t) instead of close[t] -> close[t+h]. Why: the 2026-10-11 edge study found ~90% of the ADR-0059 label's IC sits in [t, t+1], the bar a decision made after bar t closes can never trade; this walk measures what a next-bar fill can earn. Development evidence only (deployment_eligible=false by construction: same development_validation folds).",
